#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Summarize completed numerical records without opening inventory artifacts."""
import json,pathlib
C=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
summary=json.loads((C/'rehearsal/final-summary.json').read_text())
details={
'alma':('The collector failed on a root-inaccessible document-portal alias; package directories distorted file accounting, and GROUP/language-parent reasons were not valid individual reasons.','The static helper represents the portal as an opaque alias; RPM directories retain ownership only, symlink targets and valid digests are checked, and GROUP and native-parent reason inference remain unknown.'),
'void':('The collector could not start portably; action prerequisites from a rolling repository were incompatible with the old base, and immediate service checks raced startup.','Collection logic runs on the host with its static guest helper. The native package action performs documented XBPS self-update and rolling update; runit, network and engine waits are explicit. npm cowsay uses its own local lock. The four-round numerical ready claim was subsequently invalidated by independent language-reason review.'),
'gentoo':('The first pass allocated insufficient compilation capacity, and source builds, USE prerequisites, browser cleanup, user runlevels and a missing Docker CLI prevented completion. Current dependency edges had incorrectly supplied installation history.','The clone has the fixed four-slot allocation. After the allowed repair interval, an application AppImage, Python/pip cowsay and existing dhcpcd implement the same Section9.2 activities. Browser cleanup, OpenRC runtime/runlevel setup and Docker CLI were repaired. Portage marks only uniquely resolved selected records explicit; all unsupported historical reasons remain unknown.'),
'microos':('The late registered system had not been rehearsed, and published inputs named the superseded DVD rather than its active vendor image.','FX1 performed the full collector and twenty transport calls on a fresh clone. Active release provenance now names the exact plain KVM/XEN image, checksum and listing date; the DVD remains explicitly superseded.'),
'talos':('Image facts were not structured, the configured-image reason was absent, and neither complete image membership nor actual covering-mount evidence was established.','The single image object has structured facts and an explicit reason from the redacted active configuration. Bounded installed /usr listings retain file rows. All unsupported image/file integrity remains unknown; final source also retains unknown symlinks. The final measured0/95 is regular files from round14, not a rerun of later source.'),
'nixos':('The earlier transport evidence was not included consistently in final readiness.','The registered unchanged system receives a new fresh-clone sequence of twenty fixed exit-status calls; no collector, property assessment or workload is added.'),
'guix':('The initial SSH preparation failed, and the late original serial registration needed rehearsal and explicit shutdown fallback.','The registered KIT2 serial transport runs fixed status calls without inventory. Intermittent framing failures led to a short tty handshake before the wrapper, retention of the login shell, an exact shell-sync challenge, slow byte pacing, acknowledged small chunks with full checksums and checked decoding, and a closing marker gated on terminal restoration. Failed sequences terminate early and require a fresh clone; readiness still requires twenty successes. Failed graceful shutdown uses the documented kill/destroy fallback; all statuses are preserved.'),
'fedora':('The initial collector start-up and Homebrew installer download failed, and old reason/file ratios were inadequate.','The host/static-helper collector removes the guest interpreter requirement. The Homebrew installer GET has bounded retries and a temporary output file; package file accounting and conservative reason handling use the shared repaired collector. Homebrew discovery now emits an explicit unsupported-adapter gap and numeric counter; its package identities, files, reasons and integrity are not inferred. Per-round action repairs are retained in the system notes.'),
'mint':('Steam needed unattended display/bootstrap handling; SteamCMD checked an ambiguous destination, and collection had incomplete traversal/file accounting.','Steam and Lutris use private virtual displays and buses, with supervised process groups, wrapper handoff handling and bounded cleanup after controller death. SteamCMD sets its explicit destination before anonymous login. Slow APT acquisition led to bounded waits/retries and, after more than thirty minutes of repair, temporary Ubuntu-only HTTPS source copies for the same repositories and packages. FX2 was explicitly interrupted after certified action-session termination; its143 marker is operator-supplied, with no completed action invented. The GVFS alias boundary and default Flatpak preflight removed collector errors; numeric type counters distinguish unknown symlinks without opening inventory. Installed dpkg records do not provide expected symlink targets, so those integrity facts remain unknown. All action diagnoses and replacements are recorded in the system notes.'),
'debian-server':('The old file ratio counted directories, and the scripted K3s default runtime store needed an explicit opaque boundary.','All thirteen prescribed activities are retained. Directory entries establish ownership without entering the file denominator; the K3s default runtime stores are opaque. The fresh rounds use the conservative language-reason rules.'),
}
s='''# FX-C1-REH-1 repair record

Prepared 2026-11-23 UTC. This is instrument preparation, not an observation or a hypothesis outcome. Every assigned system is ready or has exhausted four repair rounds. Numeric round keys11–14 mean FX1–FX4; historical rounds remain. No fifth repair round is inferred from a later source amendment.

The repaired collector, runner and action sources are the final files identified by `input-files.sha256.tsv`. The original text, protocol and choices retain the hashes in `rehearsal/FX-SCOPE.md`. Raw rehearsal objects, query stdout and member lists were deleted unread. Allowed diagnostic reads, and an accidental exposure during independent source review, are disclosed in `DISCLOSURES.md` and `rehearsal/REVIEW-EXPOSURES.md`.

## Systems

'''
for row in summary:
 system=row['system'];wrong,repaired=details[system]
 s+='### '+system+'\n\n'+wrong+' '+repaired+'\n\n'
 whole_text=str(row['whole'])+' seconds' if row['whole'] is not None else 'not recorded'
 s+='Result: **'+('ready' if row['ready'] else 'not ready')+'**, FX'+str(row['round']-10)+'. '+row['actions']+'; '+row['collector']+'; transport '+row['transport']+'; whole '+whole_text+'.\n\n'
 s+='Remaining: '+('; '.join(row['failures']) if row['failures'] else 'no acceptance blocker; named collector scope limitations remain')+'. Evidence: '+row['evidence']+'.\n\n'
s+='''## Original review findings

| C1/REVIEW.md finding | Disposition | Evidence and reason |
|---|---|---|
|1 Stale/missing manifest inputs and old copied choices|Fixed|The documents are regenerated from completed records. DISCLOSURES reproduces the unchanged current CHOICES; the final manifest and allowlist are generated after the review and all writers stop. The independent final review exists at `rehearsal/REVIEW-FINAL.md`.|
|2 Background rehearsals and stale system rows after finalization|Fixed|Every final row names its latest completed FX round. `rehearsal/cleanup-final.tsv` records no remaining rehearsal clone or transient inventory; final generation follows cleanup.|
|3 MicroOS active image/checksum mismatch|Fixed|`releases.tsv` distinguishes the superseded DVD from the active plain Snapshot20261121 KVM/XEN image, SHA256 `fd2d22de41741d042a1b9c6a993fc9fa296ec1312083f14ea8dc0d4e58ce5826`. Listing/signature evidence is under `raw/microos-kit2/`.|
|4 MicroOS omitted despite late readiness|Fixed|`rehearsal/microos/status.tsv` and `counts.tsv` contain FX1, collector0, nonzero L2 and twenty successful calls.|
|5 Missing Gentoo/Guix records and invented counts citations|Fixed|Host numerical histories are synchronized, all new rounds retained, and READY cites only files that exist. No inventory count is invented for a transport-only system.|
|6 Missing latest-stable release evidence|Fixed|Dated Talos release metadata, official NixOS download page and newer-channel404, and Void current/enterprise listings are saved under `raw/fx-release-evidence/` with exact request URLs and retrieval times. These are post-cutoff corroborating retrievals, not falsely dated cutoff captures.|
|7 Laboratory home paths in published recipes|Fixed|Credential-free recipes use explicit root placeholders and `install/materialize.py`; no laboratory home layout is published. Literal public-key markers in reusable templates survive exact reconstruction; `rehearsal/materialize-verification.json` records13 byte-identical templates.|
|8 Unstated Talos and MicroOS image-variant choices|Not fixed in CHOICES|The lead explicitly forbids changing a choice written in CHOICES. Existing selected artifacts are identified exactly in releases and recipes, but no missing contemporaneous rationale is invented. The omitted comparison of Talos metal-amd64 against other images, and MicroOS plain against grub-bls/sdboot, remains disclosed.|
|9 Overwritten kit review reference|Fixed|The original review remains byte-identical as `REVIEW-KIT.md`; KIT-READY, KIT-SHA256SUMS and build-manifest.py now refer to it. KIT-SHA256SUMS is a historical kit snapshot; the final primary checksum manifest covers revised publication files.|

## Additional independent source review

`rehearsal/FX-INSTRUMENT-REVIEW.md` and `rehearsal/SOURCE-ACCEPTANCE.md` record the source repairs: no native-parent language reason transfer, unique Portage selected-set resolution, no unsupported Talos integrity, fresh-clone enforcement, separately retained stderr, certified timeout cleanup, confined limitation citations, strict four-round and percentage criteria, and directory/file accounting. Query exceptions require a reviewed class and retained diagnostic; caps, parser errors and unexplained failures remain failures.

Alma and Void completed their fourth rounds before the language-reason correction. Their original aggregate counts remain untouched; acceptance uses a conservative lower bound obtained by subtracting every historically known Python/npm reason. No deleted inventory is reopened or reconstructed. Gentoo FX1's obsolete graph-derived reasons are also explicitly invalidated. New rounds record the reason source categories in memory. A source correction alone cannot turn an exhausted machine into ready. Gentoo FX4 retains its browser failure after a strengthened shutdown check; the final native shutdown and second-start permanent-extension check passed source review but was not replayed after round four. Its exact staged and final helper hashes are disclosed.

Alma FX3's transitional deployment lost most aggregate counters; this is disclosed rather than reconstructed from deleted raw output. Identical duplicate numerical counters in early overlapping reducer versions remain historical records and are not added together. Finalization selects the single value per round/kind.

Section9.2 reporting remains exactly the text's rule: without the required second-level inventory, a machine cannot yield1; it yields0 only if a failure-condition object is found, otherwise?. No outcome is assigned by these rehearsals.
'''
(C/'FIX-C1-REH-1.md').write_text(s)
